<title>UK: SNAPSHOT - Top 10 EBRD members.</title>
<headline>SNAPSHOT - Top 10 EBRD members.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Founded in 1991 to promote the post-communist transition of central and eastern European to market economies, the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) has 60 contributing countries backing 20 billion ecu capital.</p>
<p>Following is a table of the subscribed capital at December 31 1996</p>
<p>				   TOTAL CAPITAL ECU 000</p>
<p> United States		 1,000,000</p>
<p> France			    851,750</p>
<p> Germany			   851,750</p>
<p> Italy			     851,750</p>
<p> Japan			     851,750</p>
<p> United Kingdom		  851,750</p>
<p> Russian Federation	    400,000</p>
<p> Canada			    340,000</p>
<p> European Community	    300,000</p>
<p> European Investment Bank    300,000</p>
<p>(Source: EBRD 1996 annual report)</p>
<p>($ = 0.880 European Currency Unit ECUs at current rates) -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
